Usage of check:
  -branch string
    	check a BRANCH instead of paths: exit 1 if another checkout has it and its owner is not provably gone
  -cwd-unknown
    	the caller's working directory is not knowable here (e.g. mcp__trixi__agent_shell): refuse relative paths instead of resolving them against the wrong base
  -gate
    	read-only deny gate: exit 1 if a foreign live claim or lock/beacon covers any path; never acquires, refreshes, or writes
  -held
    	retired (loto-ojq3): exits 0; commits are not gated
  -moved
    	advisory only: given two HEADs, print a ⚠ row for each path the move changed that a live peer holds; always exits 0
  -staged
    	read paths from git diff --cached
  -worktree string
    	check a worktree PATH instead of paths: exit 1 if another live session is working at or inside it, locks or not; exit 3 if a live session there cannot be placed
